course: dictionary
lesson: 14295
title: Nourish: food, growth and hope
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To nourish something is to give it what it needs to live, grow and stay healthy. Food nourishes the body, and soil nourishes plants. «The soil nourishes the young carrots.» The soil gives the carrots what they need, so nourish means feed and help them grow.
explain: The word can also be about the mind. «Reading nourishes the imagination.» Books help your imagination grow, just as food helps your body grow. You can also see the word on food labels and in healthy-eating lessons: «A nourishing lunch is one that is good for you.» Nourishing means healthy and good for growth.
explain: Look at the words around nourish to check its meaning. Food, soil and healthy are clues. If you can swap in help something grow and it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Nourish means to give a person, animal or plant the food it needs to live, grow and stay healthy.
fact: «Nourishing» food is healthy food, and «well nourished» means a body has been given enough good food.
fact: You can also nourish a feeling, idea or skill, so that it grows stronger: «Kindness nourishes friendship.»
fact: In a more formal sense, «nourish» can mean keeping a hope or belief alive for a long time: «She nourished the hope of seeing her father again.»
fact: A good check is to swap in the words help to grow or keep alive into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The soil in the garden nourishes the carrots and beans.» What does nourishes mean here? | Sells the plants at the market | Covers the plants with a thick blanket | *Gives the plants the food they need to grow | Makes the plants go dry and brown
exercise: «Reading good books can nourish a young writer's imagination.» What does nourish mean here? | *Help it grow stronger | Hide it away from others | Make it quiet and small | Stop it from working
exercise: «Mum packed a nourishing lunch: brown bread, eggs and an apple.» What does nourishing mean? | Sweet food that is bad for the teeth | Cold food that is left over from dinner | *Healthy food that helps the body grow and stay well | Food that is very hard to chew
test: «He nourished a hope that his lost dog would come home.» What does nourished mean here? | *Kept the hope alive for a long time | Told everyone that the hope was silly | Forgot the hope very quickly | Wrote the hope down on paper
test: «The well nourished puppies were plump and playful.» What does well nourished mean? | *Given the right food, so they are healthy and strong | Kept in a cold, dark place | Given too many sweets and treats | Left alone without any food
exam: «Kindness nourishes a friendship, just as water nourishes a plant.» What does nourishes mean in this sentence? | *Helps it grow and stay strong | Covers it with mud | Pulls it out of the ground | Breaks down slowly
